Third-party content

Source/scripts/library/Set Color from Material V3.0.py is the Set Color from
Material script by Cator, finalized with help from the Alibre Design forum
community, and is included here byte for byte as published at:

    https://www.alibre.com/forum/index.php?resources/set-color-from-material.150/

It is distributed under whatever terms its authors set on that resource page,
not under the MIT license above. The MIT license covers the add-on host, the
Alibre Script runtime in Source/scripts/bootstrap.py, the packaging and the
build tooling in this repository.

IronPython is redistributed with the installer under the Apache License 2.0:

    https://github.com/IronLanguages/ironpython2/blob/master/LICENSE

Alibre Design, AlibreX and the Alibre Script add-on are products of Alibre,
LLC. The add-on compiles against assemblies that ship with Alibre Design; none
of those assemblies are included in this repository or in the installer.
